From 6d50f198e766b3273581eb46e43ca65e006172c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:42:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 218/231] ASoC: codecs: Add an MT6369 codec driver (uplink)

The MT6369, the second PMIC of MT6858 phones, has the MT6359's audio
design behind the 8-bit registers of the SPMI PMICs. Start a mainline
driver, modelled on mt6359.c with the sequences of MediaTek's GPLv2
mt6369.c, with the uplink only: the three analog microphone inputs,
both preamplifiers and ADCs, and MTKAIF to the AFE. Its 26 MHz comes
from a clock-buffer output of the MT6685.

Tested on the Jolla Phone (2026), with the MTKAIF calibration and the
clock fixes that follow: both internal microphones record.
---
